From c7e8f2dd60902fb0971d78bf7d8ea2fb0b5c9025 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hamza <155834495+lonadonia@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:15:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/12] marianos-azure-headless 1.10.0rc6 (tests only): a page
 for the store whose product data has not loaded counts nothing and is asked
 again (OR-19)

Run F2 (1.10.0rc5) stopped with exit 7 on re-ask 1 of page 2 of Espresso Coffee: the answer's own search was
made for 53100502 Pickup, but its page state carried no product's data, and the store check took it for
another store's page. These tests replay that stored answer and state the corrected behaviour on synthetic
pages: no product counted, the answer kept with its identity and the original reason, bounded retries, a
resumable stop when they run out, recovery across a restart; a page of another store, another fulfillment or
without store proof still stops the run. Expected to fail on 1.10.0rc5 (5 tests) and pass with the fix; the
three controls pass on both.

Fixtures: byte copies of five pages the collector stored on 2026-11-16 (three of F2's Espresso Coffee answers,
and the Coupons page loaded and not loaded, used by the OR-04 tests), with their origins in SOURCES.json.
